# Typography: no em dash

Never use the em dash character (Unicode U+2014) in code, UI copy, tests, fixtures, or docs written for this project.

## Prefer

- **Missing / empty values:** `-`
- **Title or label + detail:** ` : ` (e.g. `Bulletin : Awa Kongo`, `Caisse : Frais`)
- **Lists, mottos, ranges, asides:** ` - ` (e.g. `Rigueur - Travail - Réussite`, `PDF - Word ou image`)
- **Decorative rules:** ASCII hyphens only (`-------`)

## Also avoid

- En dash (Unicode U+2013) in user-facing strings; use `-` instead.

## Examples

Bad title separator: use a colon instead of an em dash between "Bulletin" and the student name.

Bad empty placeholder: use `'-'`, never an em dash character.

Good: `Bulletin : Awa Kongo`, `value ?? '-'`, `Rigueur - Travail - Réussite`.
